1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,901
1990. Poland is the poorest country on this chart: 12,821 dollars a person,

2
00:00:07,901 --> 00:00:09,875
adjusted for prices.

3
00:00:10,275 --> 00:00:12,150
Watch the amber line.

4
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:18,600
2011. It passes Hungary.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,250
Greece's debt crisis drags its line down.

6
00:00:23,050 --> 00:00:26,225
2015. Poland passes Greece.

7
00:00:26,625 --> 00:00:28,675
Then comes the pandemic.

8
00:00:29,475 --> 00:00:32,350
2020. It passes Portugal.

9
00:00:32,750 --> 00:00:34,900
And by 2025,

10
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:39,325
Poland is at 95 percent of Spain.

11
00:00:39,725 --> 00:00:44,548
If the last ten years' pace held, it would pass Spain in about two years.

12
00:00:44,548 --> 00:00:47,125
How Poland did it is in our full video.
